tate movement\n- Total program time goal: **< 60 minutes**\n\n**5. Positioning**:\n- Perform bowel program on a **padded commode chair** if possible (gravity-assisted)\n- If in bed, use **left side-lying position** (descending colon is gravity-dependent)\n\n**6. Rescue Plan for Refractory Constipation**:\n- If no results after 3 days: **mini-enema** (docusate liquid enema)\n- If impaction suspected: manual disimpaction with lidocaine pre-treatment\n- If chronic failure despite optimization: consider **transanal irrigation system** (Peristeen) or gastroenterology referral for evaluation of colonic inertia\n- Last resort: **Malone antegrade continence enema (MACE/ACE)** procedure or colostomy for severe refractory neurogenic bowel\n\n**7. UTI Prevention Strategy**:\n- Adequate hydration (addresses both constipation and UTI risk)\n- Strict clean intermittent catheterization technique review\n- Cranberry supplements (limited evidence but low risk)\n- Avoid prophylactic antibiotics unless >3 symptomatic UTIs per year despite behavioral modifications\n- Ensure complete bladder emptying; check post-void residuals\n- Treat only **symptomatic** UTIs (not asymptomatic bacteriuria, which is expected in SCI)',
